[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5117010831","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121842#issuecomment-5117010831","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121842","id":5117010831,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMP9jjw","user":{"login":"Marigem","id":43501741,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTAxNzQx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43501741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marigem","html_url":"https://github.com/Marigem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marigem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marigem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marigem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marigem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marigem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marigem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marigem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marigem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marigem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T11:17:35Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T11:18:29Z","body":"A possible workaround seems to be handling the pause/unpause input in `_physics_process` instead of `_input`, even though I'm using call_deferred in both cases.\n\n```\nfunc _physics_process(delta: float) -> void:\n    if Input.is_action_just_pressed(\"ui_left\"):\n        call_deferred(\"toggle_paused\")\n```\nSo the root problem seems to be that even using call_deferred in _input still isn't enough to ensure an error like this doesn't happen.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5117010831/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"